course: dictionary
lesson: 12518
title: Descendants: the line that goes forward
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your descendants are the people who come after you in your family: your children, their children, and so on into the future. «Grandma's descendants filled the park for the family picnic.» Grandma is the starting point, and everyone who comes after her in the family line is a descendant.
explain: Scientists use the word too. Birds are descendants of dinosaurs, which means birds came from an older kind of living thing and changed over a very long time. «Modern dogs are descendants of wolves.» The clue is always the same: a descendant comes after something older.
explain: Look for the clue in the sentence. Ask: who or what came first? «The settlers built the village, and their descendants still live there.» The settlers came first, and their descendants came later. When you find the older thing, you have found the start of the line.
fact: Descendants means the children, grandchildren and later family who come after a person.
fact: In science, descendants are living things that come from an older kind, like birds from dinosaurs.
fact: The singular is descendant (one descendant), and the plural is descendants (more than one).
fact: «Direct descendants» means the line straight down from one person: parent, child, grandchild and so on.
fact: In formal writing, something new that grew out of something older can be called a descendant, such as modern languages from older ones.
exercise: «The king's descendants still live in the castle.» Who are the descendants? | The king's own parents | The king's servants | *People who come after the king in his family line | The people who built the castle
exercise: Birds are descendants of dinosaurs. What does this tell you? | *Birds come from an older kind of living thing | Birds and dinosaurs have always looked exactly the same | Birds and dinosaurs lived in the same place | Dinosaurs came from birds
exercise: «The settlers built the village, and their descendants still live there.» Which word tells you who came first? | village | *settlers | there | still
test: «My great-grandmother has many descendants, including me.» Who are the descendants of my great-grandmother? | *Her children, grandchildren and later family | Her friends from school | Her neighbours on the street | Her teachers
test: Modern English is a descendant of older languages. What does descendant mean here? | A word that means the same as old | A dictionary that is very old | A person who speaks English | *Something new that grew out of something older
exam: Mia says descendants means old ones. Which meaning is best? | Things that are very old and broken | *Living things, or people, that come from an older kind | Animals that only live in the sea | The oldest person in the family
